{"kind": "tool_approval", "tool": "book_chapter_save_draft", "args": {"body": "The air in the archives was thick with the scent of old parchment and the metallic tang of dying embers. Elara traced the glowing runes of the Ember Codex, her fingers trembling just enough to make the light flicker. It wasn't just a book; it was a heartbeat, pulsing with a rhythm that matched her own.

"It's waking up," she whispered, the sound swallowed by the vast, shadowed silence of the library.

Outside, the storm began to howl, but inside, the only sound was the soft, rhythmic thrum of the ancient magic. The ink on the pages seemed to shift, swirling like smoke, forming patterns that hadn't been seen in a thousand years. Elara knew that once she turned the next page, there would be no turning back. The history of the world was about to rewrite itself.", "book_id": "01a02e96-3c65-708e-b171-2336fc1952f0", "chapter": "1", "chapter_id": "01a02e96-3d2e-715a-b45d-7b2c4991edcf"}, "tier": "A"}

